course: dictionary
lesson: 9484
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word steal has several meanings. The context, meaning the words around it, shows you which one is right. The main meaning is to take something that belongs to someone else, without permission and without meaning to give it back. «A boy's birthday money was stolen at break.» That is stealing, and it is wrong.
explain: Steal can also mean moving quietly and secretly. «She stole out of the room while everyone was busy.» Nobody heard her leave, so stole means she slipped away without being seen. In sport, steal means taking the ball from the other team.
explain: Check the clues. Is someone taking something that is not theirs? Is someone moving quietly? Is it a game? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If you read «The bike for five pounds was a steal», a steal means something very cheap for what it is worth. This is an informal use, so it is not the main meaning.
fact: Steal is a verb: steal, steals, stole, stolen, stealing.
fact: «Stolen» means taken without permission and never given back.
fact: «Stole a glance» means looked quickly and secretly, as in «She stole a glance at the clock».
fact: «A steal» is informal and means something very cheap for what it is worth.
fact: If you think something has been stolen, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «She stole out of the room while everyone was busy.» What does stole mean here? | Took a prize from the teacher | *Moved quietly and secretly | Ran very fast | Shouted loudly
exercise: «A boy's birthday money was stolen at break.» What does stolen mean? | Counted carefully | *Taken without permission and never given back | Lent to a friend | Put away in a safe place
exercise: A shopper says, «The bike for five pounds was a steal.» What does a steal mean? | A theft in a dark alley | *Something very cheap for what it is worth | A strong bike lock | A sports team's win
test: «The striker stole the ball from the other team and scored.» What does stole mean in sport? | Passed the ball to a friend | Dropped the ball on the grass | Kicked the ball out of play | *Took the ball from the other team
test: «She stole a glance at the clock.» What does stole a glance mean? | Forgot what time it was | *Looked quickly and secretly | Stared at the clock for hours | Broke the clock by accident
exam: What should you do if you think a friend has stolen something? | Keep it secret and say nothing | Post it online for everyone to see | Steal it back | *Talk to them or a trusted adult
